        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract ticket details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762404693003"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_TICKET_DETAILS",
          "id": "1762404357023",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762404357024_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Objective\n\nExtract a clear, context-aware title and problem description for logging a ticket based on user query and chat history. If chatHistory is unavailable, use the userQuery. If unclear, ask for clarifying questions.\n\n---\n\n## Input Source\n\n- `userQuery`: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userQuery}}\n- `chatHistory`: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n- `selectedChoices`: {{$context.$nodes.GET_OBJECTTYPE.$output.items[0].SelectedChoices}}\n- `additionalFields`: {{$context.$nodes.PARSEADDITIONALFIELDS.$output.result}}\n- `inputObjectType`: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectType}}\n\n---\n\n### **Steps**\n\n1. **Extract Relevant Information:**\n    - From `chatHistory`, pull only the turns **related** to `userQuery` (similar topic, issue, clarification, or resolution).\n    - Ignore unrelated or repeated text. Set this to `context`.\n    - If `chatHistory` is unavailable, use only `userQuery`.\n\n2. **Include Relevant Next or Troubleshooting Steps:**\n    - If the chat history contains **relevant next steps** or **troubleshooting steps** that the user has tried and reported, include those as part of the **problemDescription**.\n    - Ensure that only steps that were tried by the user and are directly related to the issue are included.\n    - Do not include steps that have not been tried or that are irrelevant.\n\n3. **Extract Title and Problem Description:**\n    - Extract a `title` (≤400 characters) and `problemDescription` (≤1000 characters) from the relevant `context` (either from `chatHistory` or `userQuery` or both):\n      - **DO NOT INCLUDE** any PII (emails, names, user IDs, phone numbers, etc.) in either the `title` or `problemDescription`.\n      - **DO NOT INCLUDE**  any `additionalFields` in either the `title` or `problemDescription`.\n      - Remove ticket or case identifiers and action request phrases (e.g., \"log a ticket,\" \"please raise a request\").\n      - Remove details like `srId`, `ticketId`, `personId`, etc.\n      - Do not include solutions, next steps, or irrelevant information unless the user has tried and reported them.\n      - **Only include** the reported issue and relevant factual observations; avoid assumptions, extra details, or any user requests for action, investigation, escalation, or issuance.\n      - Ensure both fields are clear, concise, grammatically correct, and safe to share.\n\n4. **Determine the Object Type:**\n    - If `inputObjectType` is \"hrHelpDeskRequests\" or \"internalServiceRequests\",\n      - **Do not determine** `objectType`.\n      - set `inputObjectType` to `objectType`.  \n    - Else,\n      - If the `selectedChoices` array is empty, set `title`, `problemDescription`, `questions` and `objectType` to an empty string.\n      - If the `selectedChoices` array contains \"ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_SERVICE_REQUESTS\" only, set `objectType` to `\"internalServiceRequests\"`.\n      - If the `selectedChoices` array contains \"ORA_SVC_HR_SERVICE_REQUESTS\" only, set `objectType` to `\"hrHelpDeskRequests\"`.\n      - If the `selectedChoices` array contains BOTH \"ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_SERVICE_REQUESTS\" and \"ORA_SVC_HR_SERVICE_REQUESTS\", decide by inspecting the `problemDescription`:\n        - If `problemDescription` (case-insensitive) contains any HR-related keywords or the intent relates to HR processes, workforce matters, or employee life-cycle tasks such as joining, onboarding, offboarding, employment changes, or internal mobility:\n          - HR-related keywords include: payroll, benefit, leave, legal, confidentiality, confidential, NDA, non-disclosure, privacy, GDPR, CCPA, etc.\n          - set `objectType` to `\"hrHelpDeskRequests\"`.\n        - For all other operational or IT-related queries (e.g., technical support, facilities, equipment, issues with laptops, etc.), set `objectType` to `\"internalServiceRequests\"`.\n        - Set `questions` to an empty string.\n    - If `additionalFields` contain \"ReferenceObjectId\" or \"IBAssetId\" or contains CategoryCode related to \"Incentives\", set `objectType` to `\"internalServiceRequests\"`. (Hard override)\n\n5. **Set productProfileOptionCode**\n    - If `objectType` is \"internalServiceRequests\", set `productProfileOptionCode` to `\"SVC_ISR_PROD_CATALOG_USAGE\"`.\n    - If `objectType` is \"hrHelpDeskRequests\", set `productProfileOptionCode` to `\"SVC_HCM_PROD_CATALOG_USAGE\"`.\n\n6. **If Insufficient Context:**\n    - If the `title`, `problemDescription` lack enough context to create a valid ticket, ask 1–2 short, clear clarification questions. set it as `questions`.\n    - Do not ask for PII (e.g., email, phone, IDs).\n    - Set `title`, `problemDescription`, and `objectType` to an empty string.\n\n---\n\n### **Example Output**\n\n- **If enough context is provided:**\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Issue with payroll deduction\",\n    \"problemDescription\": \"Incorrect payroll deductions for this month. User has already tried contacting payroll support and double-checking deductions.\",\n    \"objectType\": \"hrHelpDeskRequests\",\n    \"questions\": \"\", \n    \"productProfileOptionCode\": \"SVC_HCM_PROD_CATALOG_USAGE\"    \n  }\n  ```\n\n- **If clarification is needed:**\n  ```json\n   {\n    \"title\": \"\",\n    \"problemDescription\": \"\",\n    \"objectType\": \"\",\n    \"productProfileOptionCode\": \"\",\n    \"questions\": \"[\"Can you provide more details on the issue?\", \"When did the issue first occur?\"]\"\n   }\n    ```"
            },
            {
              "id": "1762404357025_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"productProfileOptionCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"objectType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"problemDescription\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"title\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"questions\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
